ProtocolDeploy::Deployment Flow
├── Env configuration (ProtocolDeployBase)
│   ├── Given DAO_ADDRESS, SECURITY_ADDRESS, or DAO_TREASURY_ADDRESS is unset
│   │   └── It should revert (required env — critical addresses never default to the deployer)
│   ├── Given DAO_ADDRESS is the zero address
│   │   └── It should revert (sole timelock proposer; address(0) can never schedule operations)
│   ├── Given EXIT_LIQUIDITY_TARGET_ETH or CONTROLLER_RESERVE_ETH is unset
│   │   └── It should revert (required env — CREStrategyExecutor policy knobs; 0 is a valid explicit choice)
│   ├── Given TIMELOCK_ADMIN_DELAY is unset
│   │   └── It should default to the production 48h delay (sole deploy-script envOr exception)
│   ├── Given TIMELOCK_ADMIN_DELAY is set below 48h
│   │   └── It should revert (48h floor — ADMIN_ROLE trust model cannot ship with a weaker delay)
│   ├── Given TIMELOCK_ADMIN_DELAY is set to 48h or above
│   │   └── It should deploy the admin timelock with that min delay
│   ├── Given PERFORMANCE_FEE_BPS is unset
│   │   └── It should revert (required env — 0 is a valid explicit choice to disable fees)
│   └── Given GRANT_KEEPER_ROLE is unset (DeployKeeperExecutors)
│       └── It should revert (required bool — true grants in-bootstrap; false defers to timelock)
├── DeployRegistry
│   ├── It should deploy the 48h admin TimelockController (DAO proposer/canceller, security canceller, open executor)
│   ├── It should deploy the Registry with the admin timelock as its designated ADMIN_ROLE holder (never DAO_ADDRESS directly)
│   ├── It should grant SECURITY_ROLE to the security multisig (SECURITY_ADDRESS) — mirrors DeployAll
│   ├── It should leave the deployer a temporary bootstrap ADMIN_ROLE for the remaining modular steps
│   └── It should NOT finalize deployer admin (deployer needs ADMIN for later scripts)
├── Partial deploy scripts (EVE, ExitQueue, Controller, Oracle, Converter, Whitelist, AMM, Keepers)
│   ├── Each script should register its contract on Registry via _registerAndVerify
│   ├── Deployer should hold Registry ADMIN until finalize (bootstrap wiring of ADMIN-gated calls)
│   └── DeployOracle should verify the admin timelock (TIMELOCK_ADDRESS) holds ADMIN_ROLE before configuring the feed
├── Oracle feed registration guard (_assertUsdQuotedFeed — DeployOracle, DeployAll; issue #194)
│   ├── Given feed description() ends with " / USD" (Chainlink convention, incl. "Calculated <BASE> / USD")
│   │   └── It should pass and allow updateUsdFeedInfo
│   └── Given feed description() does not end with " / USD" (non-USD quote, USD as base, missing separator, arbitrary string, shorter than suffix)
│       └── It should revert the deployment with the offending description (USD-quote invariant)
├── Admin timelock delay floor (_adminTimelockDelay — DeployRegistry, DeployAll; PL-003)
│   ├── Given TIMELOCK_ADMIN_DELAY >= 48h (or unset, falling back to 48h)
│   │   └── It should deploy the admin TimelockController with that min delay
│   └── Given TIMELOCK_ADMIN_DELAY < 48h
│       └── It should revert (ADMIN_ROLE trust model cannot ship with a weaker delay)
├── DAO proposer non-zero guard (_protocolDao — DeployRegistry, DeployAll; PL-003)
│   ├── Given DAO_ADDRESS is non-zero
│   │   └── It should install that address as the sole TimelockController proposer
│   └── Given DAO_ADDRESS is address(0)
│       └── It should revert (hasRole(PROPOSER, 0) would pass but no account can schedule)
├── DeployAMM
│   ├── It should register STRATEGY_MANAGER and AMM keys
│   ├── It should initialize StrategyManager with FeeConfig (required DAO_TREASURY_ADDRESS + PERFORMANCE_FEE_BPS)
│   └── It should grant MINTER_ROLE to BOTH the AMM and the StrategyManager on Registry
├── DeployConverter
│   ├── It should register the CONVERTER key
│   ├── It should grant CONVERTER_CALLER_MANAGER_ROLE to the Converter (required for StrategyManager.addStrategy)
│   └── It should NOT call setAllowedAdapter (adapter allowlisting is always admin-timelocked after finalize)
├── DeployUniswapV3ConverterAdapter
│   ├── It should deploy UniswapV3ConverterAdapter bytecode only (no setAllowedAdapter)
│   ├── It should resolve Oracle from Registry (run after DeployOracle / DeployAll)
│   └── It is outside DeployAll (core-only); UniCL modular follow-up after finalize
├── DeployUniCLStrat
│   ├── It should deploy UniCLStrat bytecode only (no addStrategy)
│   ├── It requires Converter + a timelocked setAllowedAdapter beforehand (constructor route validation)
│   └── After deploy, addStrategy is always scheduled on the admin timelock
├── DeployAll
│   ├── It should deploy the admin timelock first and construct the Registry with it as designated admin
│   ├── It should register all Auth keys (core + QUEUE/STRATEGY_KEEPER_EXECUTOR)
│   ├── It should initialize StrategyManager with FeeConfig (required DAO_TREASURY_ADDRESS + PERFORMANCE_FEE_BPS)
│   ├── It should grant SECURITY, MINTER (AMM + StrategyManager), CONVERTER_CALLER_MANAGER on Registry
│   ├── It should deploy both keeper executors and grant them KEEPER_ROLE
│   ├── It should apply EXIT_LIQUIDITY_TARGET_ETH / CONTROLLER_RESERVE_ETH to CREStrategyExecutor
│   ├── It should verify timelock wiring (ADMIN exclusivity + timelock governance roles) separately from SECURITY_ROLE
│   ├── It should verify SECURITY / MINTER / CONVERTER_CALLER_MANAGER grants inline (Finalize uses _verifyCriticalRoleGrants)
│   ├── It should NOT deploy DEX adapters or strategies (core-only; see DeployUniswapV3ConverterAdapter / DeployUniCLStrat)
│   ├── It should NOT whitelist DEX adapters (setAllowedAdapter is always timelocked)
│   └── It should renounce the deployer's bootstrap ADMIN_ROLE after setup (ADMIN_ROLE ends held only by the timelock)
├── DeployKeeperExecutors
│   ├── It should deploy CREQueueExecutor and CREStrategyExecutor
│   ├── It should register QUEUE_KEEPER_EXECUTOR and STRATEGY_KEEPER_EXECUTOR
│   ├── It should apply EXIT_LIQUIDITY_TARGET_ETH and CONTROLLER_RESERVE_ETH (required wei env) to CREStrategyExecutor
│   └── When GRANT_KEEPER_ROLE is true (required env)
│       └── It should grant KEEPER_ROLE to both executors
│   └── When GRANT_KEEPER_ROLE is false
│       └── It should register executors without granting KEEPER_ROLE (timelock grants before finalize)
└── FinalizeProtocolDeploy
    ├── It should renounce the deployer's bootstrap ADMIN_ROLE (always — PL-003)
    ├── It should verify the admin timelock (TIMELOCK_ADDRESS) holds ADMIN_ROLE
    ├── It should verify every critical grant (SECURITY_ROLE → security, MINTER_ROLE → AMM + StrategyManager,
    │   CONVERTER_CALLER_MANAGER_ROLE → Converter, KEEPER_ROLE → both executors) and fail loudly on any gap
    ├── It should revert when a modular step was skipped (unregistered Registry key, including WHITELIST)
    └── Deployer should not be able to register contracts afterward

ProtocolDeploy::DeployScripts (integration tests)
├── test_DeployAll_RegistryAdminIsTimelockWithDaoProposer
└── test_ModularFlow_EndToEndGrantsAndFinalizeGuards
    ├── Happy path: full modular flow ends with every critical grant verified
    ├── Finalize reverts when the DeployConverter step was skipped (unregistered CONVERTER key)
    ├── Finalize reverts when the DeployWhitelist step was skipped (unregistered WHITELIST key)
    ├── Finalize reverts when the DeployKeeperExecutors step was skipped (unregistered executor key)
    └── Finalize reverts when a registered module misses a grant (StrategyManager MINTER_ROLE)

ProtocolDeploy::DeployerAdminAccess (integration tests)
├── test_FinalizeDeployerTieredAccess_RenouncesDeployerAdmin
├── test_FinalizeDeployerTieredAccess_WorksWhenRegistryPaused
├── test_FinalizeDeployerTieredAccess_IsIdempotentWhenAlreadyRenounced
├── test_FinalizeDeployerTieredAccess_DeployerCanRegisterBeforeFinalize
├── test_FinalizeDeployerTieredAccess_DeployerCannotRegisterAfterFinalize
├── test_FinalizeDeployerTieredAccess_AdminCanRegisterAfterFinalize
└── test_FullDeploymentFlow_WithSeparateDaoAndDeployer
